# Settings and Books are tabs on the bar, not also tiles, so at the default
# text size the first page of the grid reaches Daily Brief; at the largest it
# is a page further on. The pages turn both ways.
wait-for Cobalt
expect App Store
expect Terminal
expect Apps
expect Books
expect Settings
expect Kobo reader
wait-for 1 of
shot launcher-home
tap-id next
wait-for 2 of
shot launcher-page-two
tap-id previous
wait-for 1 of
# A Store app's starting screen says what it reaches for in words.
tap-paged Daily Brief
wait-for Starting
expect Connects to online services
expect-missing Uses network
shot launcher-starting-brief
tap Back
wait-for Cobalt
expect-missing Starting
# The Settings tab starts Settings and says what it changes, with the same
# way back if it never takes the panel.
tap-id settings
wait-for Starting
expect Changes the device's Wi-Fi and Bluetooth radios.
shot launcher-starting-settings
tap Back
wait-for Cobalt
# The Apps tab is the grid itself, on the page it was left at.
tap-id home
wait-for Cobalt
maybe-tap-id previous
wait-for 1 of
expect App Store
# Opening an app and coming back: the simulator runs only the launcher, so
# going behind and returning stands in for the app taking the panel. The
# list is back at once, and the app left open is marked Resume.
tap Terminal
wait-for Starting
expect Runs commands on this device.
lifecycle background
lifecycle foreground
wait-for Resume
expect-missing Starting
expect App Store
shot launcher-resume
# Every page turns forward to the last app in the catalogue.
tap-paged Verses
wait-for Starting
tap Back
wait-for Cobalt
expect Verses
